WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.666
The next day Hathi lifted his trunk.

2
00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:13.671
"Let's go!" he called, and then he and his three sons set out.

3
00:00:13.672 --> 00:00:19.110
The elephants marched in different directions.

4
00:00:19.111 --> 00:00:23.840
They reached the villagers' fields and marched around for days.

5
00:00:23.841 --> 00:00:30.211
They stomped on grass, crops, tools, and anything else they found.

6
00:00:30.212 --> 00:00:35.990
At first the other jungle creatures watched the elephants' march from a distance.

7
00:00:35.991 --> 00:00:40.624
Then birds flew over the jungle, spreading the news.

8
00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:46.640
"Food! Food for everyone!"

9
00:00:46.641 --> 00:00:51.767
Soon herds of deer, pigs, and porcupines joined the elephants.

10
00:00:51.768 --> 00:00:55.892
They all began eating what was left of the crops.

11
00:00:55.893 --> 00:01:01.416
Baloo came and found some tasty roots. "Delicious!"

12
00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:06.416
Other animals knocked down barley and drank from the tank of water.

13
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:09.840
Birds flew down for seeds and grain.

14
00:01:09.841 --> 00:01:17.950
Monkeys scattered as the python Kaa slithered into the valley. He was hungry too.

15
00:01:17.951 --> 00:01:23.881
On and on, round and round the fields, the elephants marched.

16
00:01:23.882 --> 00:01:29.049
Soon the people in the village grew desperate from hunger.

17
00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.790
"There are no more crops," a villager said.

18
00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:37.148
"We must look for food in the jungle."

19
00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:41.677
A group of people entered the jungle to look for nuts.

20
00:01:41.678 --> 00:01:51.034
But shadows with glaring eyes spooked them, and they ran out.

21
00:01:51.035 --> 00:01:57.939
By the time the rainy season came, the four elephants had finished their work in the fields.

22
00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:02.717
They began marching toward the villagers' huts.

23
00:02:02.718 --> 00:02:06.523
"What are they doing now?" Bagheera asked Mowgli.

24
00:02:06.524 --> 00:02:11.242
"They're going to rip off the huts' roofs," Mowgli said.

25
00:02:11.243 --> 00:02:15.936
Most of the villagers had already left to find new homes.

26
00:02:15.937 --> 00:02:22.750
Now it was time for the rest to go.

27
00:02:22.751 --> 00:02:27.744
A month later Mowgli and Bagheera returned to the village.

28
00:02:27.745 --> 00:02:35.182
The place was covered with mounds of grass and thick weeds.

29
00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:39.187
Six months later the two of them came back again.

30
00:02:39.188 --> 00:02:43.650
By now the jungle had roared back.

31
00:02:43.651 --> 00:02:48.523
"It's just as I imagined, Bagheera," Mowgli whispered.

32
00:02:48.524 --> 00:02:54.856
The wild jungle had swallowed up every trace of the people's village.

33
00:02:54.857 --> 00:02:59.701
After the elephants' march, Mowgli returned to the wolves' cave.

34
00:02:59.702 --> 00:03:04.045
He had found a way to punish the villagers for their cruelty.

35
00:03:04.046 --> 00:03:10.716
According to the law of the jungle, this punishment settled things.

36
00:03:10.717 --> 00:03:14.501
Yet Mowgli was restless and unhappy.

37
00:03:14.502 --> 00:03:18.620
He didn't feel hungry and he rarely slept.

38
00:03:18.621 --> 00:03:23.689
"What's wrong with me?" he wondered.

39
00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:28.226
One hot day Mowgli was splashing in the river.

40
00:03:28.227 --> 00:03:36.987
Suddenly eager to escape, he took off through the jungle, leaping from tree to tree.

41
00:03:36.988 --> 00:03:51.958
He ran all afternoon—singing, swimming, and hunting.

42
00:03:51.959 --> 00:03:57.027
At last he found himself in a strange part of the jungle.

43
00:03:57.028 --> 00:04:03.191
Near a marsh at the outskirts of a village, he heard several dogs barking.

44
00:04:03.192 --> 00:04:07.833
"A man pack!" Mowgli thought.

45
00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:14.277
Curious, he crept toward the sound of the barking dogs.

46
00:04:14.278 --> 00:04:17.933
They were pacing around in front of a hut.

47
00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:23.790
Mowgli growled like a wolf, and they instantly stopped barking.

48
00:04:23.791 --> 00:04:27.541
Then a woman came to the door.

49
00:04:27.542 --> 00:04:32.409
She wore copper bracelets, and her hair was slightly gray.

50
00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:37.155
"Who's there?" she called. Her voice shook with fear.

51
00:04:37.156 --> 00:04:40.801
"Is it another jackal?" she asked the dogs.

52
00:04:40.802 --> 00:04:46.690
As he gazed at her, Mowgli felt himself begin to shake too.

53
00:04:46.691 --> 00:04:50.933
The woman looked a bit older, but he knew her voice.

54
00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:54.494
In fact, he knew it well!

55
00:04:54.495 --> 00:05:01.277
"Messua?" he called. He stepped out of the tall grass that had been hiding him.

56
00:05:01.278 --> 00:05:04.796
The woman gasped and put a hand on her heart.

57
00:05:04.797 --> 00:05:16.213
"Nathoo? Is that you—my son?"

